# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Each model was trained on one NVIDIA V100 GPU of the Lassen
# supercomputer for up to 12 hours of wall time (some for an additional 12
# hours). Training time per model is not given individually.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Table S1 marks options with check marks rendered as '3' (yes) and '7' (no) in the text layer; only the number of layers (NequIP) and the MACE correlation order v (encoded as bodyOrder, as nu_max elsewhere) are encoded, and the optimiser variants are kept in the model labels. MACE L (maximum irrep order) has no hyperparameter individual.
# - Table S6 lists the v = 2, L = 3 model twice (duplicate for visual grouping); it is encoded once. The 'rescaling' ablation models of Tables S2 and S5 have no test errors in Tables S3/S6.
# - The 3BPA reference data (Ref. [28]) and the 3BPA test sizes are not restated here. Loss entropies and MD times to failure are not error metrics.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
